  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The system's performance and practical utility were evaluated solely through descriptive case studies rather than formal user testing.",
      "what": "The authors developed Reveal, a visual analytics platform designed to query and process heterogeneous urban data combining text and images. The system lets users construct search pipelines, apply set operations across coordinated views, and record analytical provenance. The tool's capabilities were tested across two case studies focused on urban accessibility and walkability.",
      "why": "It enables practitioners to track, reproduce, and structure complex multi-step analytical workflows when exploring subjective multimodal urban datasets."
